.TH SKIPPY-WL 1 "" "skippy-wl" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
skippy-wl \- window overview for labwc
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B skippy-wl \-\-daemon
.br
.B skippy-wl
.RB { \-\-toggle | \-\-show }
.RB [ \-\-app\-id
.IR LIST ]
.RB [ \-\-title
.IR LIST ]
.RB [ \-\-status
.IR LIST ]
.RB [ \-\-next | \-\-prev ]
.br
.B skippy-wl \-\-switch
.RB [ \-\-app\-id
.IR LIST ]
.RB [ \-\-title
.IR LIST ]
.RB [ \-\-status
.IR LIST ]
.br
.B skippy-wl \-\-quit
.br
.B skippy-wl \-\-version
.SH DESCRIPTION
Shows a fullscreen overlay with a thumbnail of every window on every output.
Windows are ordered most recently used first (as seen by the running daemon). Pick one to focus it. Windows on other workspaces and minimized windows are listed too.
.PP
Run one daemon, then bind
.B skippy-wl \-\-toggle
to a key in the compositor. Without a daemon,
.B \-\-show
and
.B \-\-toggle
show the overlay once in their own process.
.PP
Needs these Wayland protocols: ext-foreign-toplevel-list, ext-image-capture-source,
ext-image-copy-capture, wlr-foreign-toplevel-management and wlr-layer-shell.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B \-\-daemon
Track windows and listen on the control socket until
.BR \-\-quit ,
SIGINT or SIGTERM.
.TP
.B \-\-toggle
Open the overlay, or close it if it is open.
.TP
.B \-\-show
Open the overlay. Does nothing if it is open.
.TP
.B \-\-switch
Focus the previous window at once and draw nothing: the second window in the usage order, or the first if no window has focus.
.br
Takes the filters below, so
.I \-\-switch \-\-app\-id kitty
flips between the last two kitty windows.
.br
Needs the daemon. Does nothing if the overlay is open. Ignores
.B switch.pivot
and
.BR switch.wait .
.TP
.B \-\-quit
Stop the daemon.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the version.
.SH SWITCH MODE
.TP
.B \-\-next
Open on the previous window (second in the order). Hold the modifier of the key binding, press
.B Tab
to step forward, or run
.B \-\-next
again. Run
.B \-\-prev
to step back. Release the modifier to focus the selected window.
.TP
.B \-\-prev
Open on the last window. Run it again to step back.
.PP
If the modifier is released before
.B switch.wait
passes, the window is focused without drawing the overlay. With no modifier held, the switch happens at once.
.SH FILTERS
.BR \-\-show ,
.B \-\-toggle
and
.B \-\-switch
take filters that limit which windows are listed. All given filters must match.
.TP
.BI \-\-app\-id " LIST"
Match the window's app id (the class), for example
.IR kitty,foot .
.TP
.BI \-\-title " LIST"
Match the window title, for example
.IR "*vim*" .
.TP
.BI \-\-status " LIST"
Match the window state:
.BR minimized ,
.BR maximized ,
.BR fullscreen
or
.BR activated .
.PP
A
.I LIST
is comma separated glob patterns (* ? [...]), case insensitive; spaces around terms are ignored and \\, is a literal comma. A window matches if it matches any plain term and none of the terms that start with
.BR ! .
Examples:
.IR "\-\-app\-id 'kitty,foot'" ,
.IR "\-\-app\-id '!firefox'" ,
.IR "\-\-status minimized" ,
.IR "\-\-app\-id kitty \-\-status '!minimized'" .
.PP
A window whose state is not known (the compositor gave no matching handle) never matches a
.B \-\-status
filter. Nothing is shown if no window matches. Quote patterns so the shell does not expand them.
.SH OVERLAY KEYS
Defaults. Change them with
.B [bind]
in the config file.
.TP
.B Left Right Up Down
Move the selection.
.TP
.B Home End
First or last window.
.TP
.B Tab, Shift+Tab
Next or previous window.
.TP
.B Return
Focus the selected window.
.TP
.B Delete
Close the selected window.
.TP
.B m
Minimize the selected window, or restore it if it is minimized. Minimized windows are dimmed.
.TP
.B Escape
Close the overlay.
.PP
Mouse: hover selects, left click focuses, middle click closes the window, left click on empty space closes the overlay.
.SH CONFIGURATION
.I ~/.config/skippy-wl/config
(or
.IR $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/skippy-wl/config ).
One
.I key = value
per line, grouped under
.I [section]
headers. A line that starts with
.B #
is a comment, and so is the rest of a line after a
.B #
that follows whitespace. Lines may be up to 255 characters. A key outside a section is an error. The settings below are named
.IR section.key . The file is read each time the overlay opens. Invalid lines are reported on stderr and skipped.
.TP
.B layout.margin
Pixels between the screen edge and the grid. Default 48.
.TP
.B layout.spacing
Pixels between tiles. Default 28.
.TP
.B layout.label_height
Pixels reserved under each tile for the title. Default 28.
.TP
.B layout.label
Text under each tile:
.BR title ,
.B app_id
or
.BR both .
Default
.IR title .
.TP
.B monitors.mode
.B each
shows the windows of each monitor on that monitor.
.B pointer
shows all windows on the monitor the pointer enters when the overlay opens; the other monitors stay empty.
Default
.IR each .
.TP
.B switch.pivot
switch mode: focus the selected window when the modifiers held at open are released.
.B false
leaves the overlay open until Enter, a click or Escape. Default
.IR true .
.TP
.B switch.wait
Milliseconds to wait before drawing the overlay in switch mode (needs
.BR switch.pivot ).
0 draws at once. Default 100.
.TP
.B icons.enabled
.B true
draws the application icon in the corner of each tile, and large in the middle of tiles without a thumbnail. Default
.IR true .
.TP
.B icons.size
Size in pixels, 16 to 256, of the corner icon. Default 48. Tiles smaller than three times this have no corner icon. Tiles without a thumbnail show a larger icon sized to the tile.
.TP
.B icons.theme
Icon theme name. Its parents and
.B hicolor
are searched too. Default
.IR hicolor .
.TP
.B animation.enabled
.B true
fades the overlay in and grows the tiles slightly when it opens. Default
.IR true .
.TP
.B animation.duration
Milliseconds the open animation takes, 0 to 1000. 0 shows the overlay at once. Default 150.
.TP
.B layout.font
Pango font description for titles. Default
.IR "Sans 11" .
.TP
.B colors.background
Overlay color as #RRGGBB or #RRGGBBAA. Default #000000ff.
.TP
.B colors.highlight
Selection color as #RRGGBB or #RRGGBBAA. Default #5999ff.
.TP
.B colors.border
Border of unselected tiles, #RRGGBB or #RRGGBBAA. Default #ffffff2e.
.TP
.B colors.theme_file
Labwc theme file, read each time the overlay opens. Only a leading
.B ~/
is expanded. The selected tile uses
.B window.active.border.color
and other tiles use
.B window.inactive.border.color
at 60% alpha.
.B colors.highlight
and
.B colors.border
in the config file win. Example:
.IR ~/.local/share/themes/noctalia/openbox-3/themerc .
.TP
.B bind.select bind.cancel bind.close bind.minimize bind.left bind.right bind.up bind.down bind.home bind.end bind.next bind.prev
Keys of the [bind] section, for example
.IR "select = Return" .
Up to four xkb keysym names, comma separated. A line replaces the default keys of that action. A key moves from its old action to the new one.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/skippy-wl.sock
Control socket of the daemon.
.TP
.I PREFIX/share/skippy-wl/skippy-wl.conf
Config template.
.SH LABWC
In
.IR ~/.config/labwc/autostart :
.PP
.nf
skippy-wl \-\-daemon &
.fi
.PP
In
.IR ~/.config/labwc/rc.xml :
.PP
.nf
<keybind key="A\-Tab">
  <action name="Execute" command="skippy\-wl \-\-toggle"/>
</keybind>
.fi
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success, 1 on any error.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR labwc (1)
